[I] High performance C++ numeric library

[T] Blitz++ is a C++ class library for scientific computing which provides
[T] performance on par with Fortran 77/90. It uses template techniques to
[T] achieve high performance. The current versions provide dense arrays and
[T] vectors, random number generators, and small vectors and matrices.

[A] Todd Veldhuizen <tveldhui@oonumerics.org>
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[U] https://github.com/blitzpp/blitz/wiki

[C] extra/development
[F] CROSS

[L] Artistic

[V] 1.0.2

[D] 3d8bcaeace1f4f57a2a747ed1fda818a8a6c1a0ef06642921fe94b52 blitz-1.0.2.tar.gz https://github.com/blitzpp/blitz/archive/1.0.2/

autogen=1

blitz_host_generators() {
	mkdir -p $builddir/host-gen
	for x in blitz/generate/gen*.cpp; do
		x=${x##*/}
		$BUILDCXX -O2 -Iblitz/generate blitz/generate/$x -o $builddir/host-gen/${x%.cpp}
	done
}
atstage cross && hook_add preconf 5 blitz_host_generators
atstage cross && var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DBLITZ_HOST_GENERATORS=$builddir/host-gen
